all code"}, {"side": "buyer", "title": "Open lower and use the shop\'s own recent price spread", "what": "Set the first offer to the lower edge of the middle half (lamp 100, chair 180, bookshelf 260) or the shop\'s own recent deal median, whichever is lower. Keep the 40%-of-gap raise and the three-offer rule. A shop that sold to others at 180 should not get 188.", "evidence": "\'ggari-shop chair: paid 188, it sold at 180 to others; asks [229, 203] offers [178, 188]\'. We paid 4% more than the public ledger shows for that shop, and we average 83.3% of budget.", "expected": "Lower average price paid, about 2-4% under the current spend, with roughly the same deal rate because 11im, dragonash and JangSeongWoong already sell at these medians.", "risk": "Some shops may reject the lowest opening. We may spend one more offer per negotiation.", "honest": "We offer only what is below our budget. We make no claim about other buyers; we use only the public ledger and our own memory.", "test": "Compare the price paid relative to the shop\'s 3-hour median and the deal rate over 40 trades, for example in 20 trades with the new rule and 20 with the old.", "effort": "small code"}]}'
