p\'s first ask is at or below min(budget, median), accept it at once, or send the exact ask, instead of running offers. Only negotiate when the ask is above the median by more than the minimum step.", "evidence": "dragonash \'says: 255 is too low. Counteroffer: 260.\' and mjforge \'promo price: 100. Listed asking price: 100.\' show many shops hold firm at the median, so extra offers cost trades but gain nothing. Our buyer averages 82.3% of budget paid, mostly because budgets are above the median.", "expected": "Fewer offers and fewer timeouts; price paid stays near the median. Round-trip speed improves, which feeds the speed sub-score.", "risk": "Sometimes a shop would have conceded 3-5 more; we leave small amounts on the table.", "honest": "The buyer pays a price it would accept, within budget and the 1.1 x upper-quartile cap, and states facts in its review.", "test": "Compare average price paid versus the median and the offers per deal, with and without the rule, over 100 trades each.", "effort": "small code"}]}'
